content.text:
{"action":"call","worker":"writer","instruction":"Using the findings from researcher (market) and researcher-2 (practical side) below, write a one-page action plan for a small cafe starting to sell coffee beans online. Include: (1) a short market summary (competitors, price points of about $14-20 per 12 oz bag, typical customers); (2) a step-by-step launch plan (product range, pricing, packaging with degassing valves, shipping options and freshness, labelling and allergen statement, registration and sales tax checks, insurance, and a test launch); (3) a main risks table with mitigations (freshness complaints, shipping damage, labelling errors, unclear registration and tax duties, cross-border costs, and thin market data). Mark unverified figures clearly, and state that the cafe's country is unknown and local legal advice is needed. Keep it to one page.

Researcher findings: Competitors are Trade, Atlas Coffee Club, Bean Box, Misto (subscriptions) and Blue Bottle, Stumptown, Onyx, Counter Culture (single roasters). Prices per 12 oz: supermarket $8-14, entry specialty and subscriptions $14-20, premium single-origin $20-30. Shipping fees about $3.99-5 on subscription sites. Customers value taste and quality first, then price and origin; subscribers want regular supply; whole-bean buyers care about roast profile; buyers expect farm, region and process details. Purchase frequency data is unreliable. Product liability insurance is about $500-1,500/year (single source). Data is US-focused and mostly from blogs with affiliate links.

Researcher-2 findings: USPS Ground Advantage is about $4-6 for 12 oz, 2-5 days; FedEx Ground $10-15; FedEx residential surcharge $6.45 (2026 schedule). Use one-way degassing valves in opaque high-barrier pouches; ship within 24-48 hours of roasting. Sturdy cartons and moisture-proof liners. Valve bags about $0.35-0.45 each (vendor claim). US labelling: product name, net weight, ingredients, business name and address, allergen statement (nine major allergens). A cafe is commonly exempt from FDA facility registration as a retail establishment, but shipping across states may add requirements; confirm with a regulator. Sales tax permit may be needed. Check whether existing insurance covers commercial food sales. Cross-border shipping is costly with duties and delays; no authoritative source found."}

